# Project Configuration

## Developer Identity
- **GitHub Username**: `prd-nguyen-trancong`
- **Go Module Path**: `github.com/prd-nguyen-trancong/gemini-tools`
- When creating Go imports, always use `github.com/prd-nguyen-trancong/gemini-tools/...`
- When pushing code to git, use the developer's own git config (do NOT modify git user.name or user.email)

## Browser Data Separation
- **Python/Playwright** browser profile: `.browser-data/gemini/` (CDP port **9222**)
- **Go/Rod** browser profile: `.browser-data/gemini-go/` (CDP port **9223**)
- These are completely separate sessions. Login must be done independently for each.
- Python and Go daemons can run in parallel without conflict.

## Go Tools
- Go module is at `go-dev-tools/`
- Build: `cd go-dev-tools && make build`
- Binaries output to `go-dev-tools/bin/`
- Shell wrappers in `bin/go-ai-*` set `PROJECT_ROOT` env var

## Python Tools
- Python tools are at `tools/gemini/` and `tools/story/`
- Run via `poetry run python -m tools.gemini.fast_ask ...`
- Shell wrappers in `bin/ai-*`
